wifi: mt76: mt7925: route BA command to WA processor for AMPDU

mt7925_mcu_sta_ba sends the STA_REC_BA TLV using MCU_UNI_CMD which
routes only to the WM (WiFi Manager) processor. The WA (WiFi Agent)
processor, which handles TX aggregation scheduling, never learns
about the BA session. As a result, firmware accepts the BA command
but never performs AMPDU framing - all TX Length counters remain
zero in AP mode despite BA sessions being established.

mt7996 sends the same TLV using MCU_WMWA_UNI_CMD which routes to
both WM and WA. Use the same command routing so WA can enable AMPDU
TX aggregation after BA setup.

Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <floss@jetm.me>

ffc0b45b68310fd35bb1ef59abcfbbaee7d07cb5
diff --git a/mt7925/mcu.c b/mt7925/mcu.c
index 360cc4d..d40eac5 100644
--- a/mt7925/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7925/mcu.c
@@ -673,7 +673,7 @@ mt7925_mcu_sta_ba(struct mt76_dev *dev, struct mt76_vif_link *mvif,
 	ba->tid = params->tid;
 
 	return mt76_mcu_skb_send_msg(dev, skb,
-				     MCU_UNI_CMD(STA_REC_UPDATE), true);
+				     MCU_WMWA_UNI_CMD(STA_REC_UPDATE), true);
 }
 
